WARNING:MISPLACED_INIT: __initdata should be placed after resource_release_param[RESOURCE_RELEASE_PARAM_SIZE]
#111: FILE: arch/x86/pci/common.c:457:
+static char __initdata resource_release_param[RESOURCE_RELEASE_PARAM_SIZE] = {0};

It is possible to use section markers on variables in a way
which gcc doesn't understand (or at least not the way the
developer intended)::

  static struct __initdata samsung_pll_clock exynos4_plls[nr_plls] = {

does not put exynos4_plls in the .initdata section. The __initdata
marker can be virtually anywhere on the line, except right after
"struct". The preferred location is before the "=" sign if there is
one, or before the trailing ";" otherwise.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/1377655732.3619.19.camel@joe-AO722/

